"""Deli Counter 0.237.0: a hole in a floor is an optional route -- left out on request, and the deli family keeps a
variant without one (the factory's roadmap 269).

The walker, 2026-10-20: "stairs and ladders should be the primary way to get between floors in this game...with the
holes in floors being somewhat rare...but still at our disposal to use if needed/desired to add some more ways to
navigate levels". Measured first (`docs/findings/hole_frequency/`): every corner-deli level carried the deli's cut drop
-- both themeable deli variants had one -- and every single-building level whose preset authors one. Level Factory
decides per level whether one is wanted; this gives it what it needs from here.

What it changes (anchored; each file pinned by hash; nothing written on a miss):
  * hole_causes.py -- `without_holes(spec)`: every drop a player would see goes (not one into a stair's own well),
    with the authored slab holes under it on every storey.
  * presets.py -- `make(..., holes=None)`: False builds the recipe without them, before every other pass.
  * new_level.py -- `--holes on|off`.
  * migrate_hole_free_variants.py (new) -- HOLE_FREE = ("deli_a01",), a call meant to be changed; run once, its
    result is specs/deli_a01.json below (the drop at (8.5, -4) and its slab hole gone, the refurnish moving nothing).
  * specs/deli_a01.json -- that result.
  * test_optional_holes.py (new, 10; all fail on 0.236.1) and test_hole_causes.py's library test.
  * VERSION 0.236.1 -> 0.237.0, CHANGELOG.
hole_causes.py and presets.py are geometry sources: `build.py --all` after this, then the suite and check.py.

Generated by `patches/dc_optional_holes/gen_dc_optional_holes.py` from a proven clone; its dry runs, the prove run, the
suites and the rebuild's records are beside it.

    python patches/patch_dc_optional_holes.py
"""
